# openOODA AArch64 Per-Feature Port Plan

Logline: A port plan that maps every x86_emit_<feature>.oo to its aarch64 twin, ranks missing ports by fixture blast radius, and gives a 5-spec top-level work list that closes the 14-row 0/3 coverage gap from the contract audit.

Setup: Companion to `openOODA/audit/aarch64-contract-coverage.oot` (16 features, 0 with 3/3, 14 with 0/3), `openOODA/audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot` (5-turn plan, 16 new matcher files in Turn 1), `openOODA/audit/aarch64-std-surface.oot` (must-wire set in std/hw/arch_aarch64/), and `openOODA/audit/x86-std-surface.oot` (x86 must-wire mirror). Static analysis only. No .oo file was modified by this RFC.

Beats:
  1. Capture the current aarch64 emit ladder: 13 oodac files, 1 per-feature file (aarch64_emit_if.oo), 0 fully-covered features.
  2. Build the 16-row per-feature port table from the contract-coverage audit, with x86 file, aarch64 Y/N, priority, and effort.
  3. Write a port spec for the top 5 HIGH-priority missing files: let, if, fn-call, int, string. Each spec names source, target, difficulty, deps.
  4. Rank the 5 HIGH ports by fixture impact; the order is the order in which to land them.
  5. List open questions for the implementer and the audit curator.

residual: The contract-gate additions from audit/aarch64-contract-coverage.oot §5 (14 KW arms) are out of scope here; they belong to a sibling RFC.

File: openOODA/rfcs/0015-aarch64-port-plan.oot
Status: Draft
Context: Tier 0 backend parity; feeds RFC 0011 / 0014 (x86 AST pipeline) shape on the aarch64 side.

